From f1104bd5b8fc6391fe70e3553ed2d9149ce8c59c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kshot3000 <kshot9000@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:31:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix fee underestimation on multi-input sends + relay cleanup

- Add txVBytes(nIn,nOut) (P2TR sizes: 41B input / 43B output / 66B witness)
  and recompute the fee for the actual input count during coin selection.
  The old fixed 169 vB estimate underpaid ~22k atoms per extra input at
  the observed std rate (and overpaid 15 vB on 1-in/2-out sends).
- getBlockHeight(): query the blockbook status endpoint instead of
  /block-index/1 (which returns the block at height 1, not the tip).
- README: drop dead link to buildandtestppg/pearl-htlc (repo does not exist).
- Regenerate stale package-lock.json (was pinned to v0.1.0 vs pkg 0.4.4).
- Add test/fee.test.mjs (24/24 pass): hand-computed vbyte table,
  validation errors, wire-format cross-check vs buildTx() serialization,
  old-estimate shortfall quantification.

Verified: node test/fee.test.mjs 24/24, security 25/25, vault 6/6,
rotation 8/8 PASS; vite build PASS. (system/vectors suites need live
network / Go reference fixture - environmental.)
---
 README.md            |   2 +-
 package-lock.json    | 422 +++++++++++++++++++++++++------------------
 package.json         |   2 +-
 src/App.jsx          |  39 ++--
 src/lib/blockbook.js |   9 +-
 src/lib/pearl.js     |  15 ++
 test/fee.test.mjs    |  61 +++++++
 7 files changed, 361 insertions(+), 189 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/fee.test.mjs

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 93ad190..44ae8b8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ Deploy target is Vercel (`vercel.json`, Node 22 for the api fns). `deploy.sh` sh
 - [ ] Post-quantum XMSS address support (Pearl's optional PQ scheme)
 - [ ] SPV / trustless balance verification
 - [ ] P2P "Buy PRL" escrow (tapscript 2-of-2) — onboarding without SafeTrade
-- [ ] PRL ↔ BTC atomic swaps (HTLC primitives already proven on-chain: [pearl-htlc](https://github.com/buildandtestppg/pearl-htlc))
+- [ ] PRL ↔ BTC atomic swaps
 
 ## Contributing
 
